    "name": "Base Payment Finance: clearing catch-up 116-119, sweep locked InvoiceMate Safe, migrate roles to new Safe",
    "description": "Executed by the Kasu multisig 0xC3128d734563E0d034d3ea177129657408C09D35 on the Payment Finance pool 0xB6DeAb2f712eFC9DF8c1E949b194BEE12F9C04FE. EXECUTION WINDOW: only between Thu 2026-09-24 06:00 UTC and Tue 2026-09-29 06:00 UTC, while isClearingTime() is FALSE. Outside it the batch REVERTS at the repayOwedFunds step: isLendingPoolClearingPending stays true whenever the pool's nextLendingPoolClearingEpoch has caught up to the current epoch and the clearing window is open. (1-4) doClearing for epochs 116/117/118/119, none of which ran (nextLendingPoolClearingEpoch=116). Once the epoch has rolled to 120 all four are past epochs, so isPastClearingTime short-circuits each to ENDED after step 1: interest only, no request processing, no step-5 draw. drawAmount=0 and isConfigOverridden=false reinforce that no funds can reach the dead Safe. Must run in ascending order. Booking 4 epochs of interest adds ~11,299 USDC to what the borrower owes (~1,130 fees / ~10,169 lenders). (5) repayOwedFunds pulls 4,937.916389 USDC from the locked InvoiceMate Safe 0x793DAEec8293A6869b42cc56988b6780f458d4f3 via its residual 78,144.736369 allowance to the LendingPoolManager; that Safe is 3-of-3 with a lost signer key and can no longer transact. Fees are paid first, so ~2,239 clears feesOwedAmount and ~2,699 reduces principal and stays in the pool as its only available liquidity. (6) updateDrawRecipient moves the draw recipient off the dead Safe onto 0x156aea25b5C62210Ea42F0A08791253688705eC9. (7-12) grant ROLE_POOL_MANAGER / ROLE_POOL_FUNDS_MANAGER / ROLE_POOL_CLEARING_MANAGER to the new Safe, then revoke the same three from the old one. ROLE_POOL_ADMIN is deliberately NOT granted - the old Safe never held it. ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: repayOwedFunds requires the OLD Safe to still hold ROLE_POOL_FUNDS_MANAGER (it is the repaymentAddress), so the sweep must precede the revokes and the clearings must precede the sweep. Atomicity is the point: there is no state in which the old roles are revoked but the sweep did not land.",
